    "title": "Skyway Bridge reopens after 'suspicious vehicle' not deemed a threat - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Bea Anhuci ,\n12 hours ago Law enforcement closed all lanes of the Bob Graham Sunshine Skyway Bridge on Wednesday morning to investigate a box found inside a \"suspicious vehicle,\" according to the Hillsborough County Sheriff's Office. The bridge has since reopened. [ Florida Department of Transportation ] All lanes of the Bob Graham Sunshine Skyway Bridge are reopened after law enforcement closed the span Wednesday to investigate a “suspicious vehicle,” according to the Hillsborough County Sheriff’s Office.\nAbout 9:45 a.m., deputies responded to the bridge after “locating a suspicious vehicle,” a spokesperson for the agency said in a statement. The sheriff’s office bomb team was called to examine a box inside the vehicle, and the Florida Highway Patrol shut down the bridge around 11 a.m.\nThe contents of the box were determined not to be a threat, and the bridge was reopened shortly before 12:30 p.m.\nNo further information was released.\nTimes staff writer Emily Wunderlich contributed to this report.\n2",
